Flowcontrol Statements in python are used to control the order in which statements executed in the program.

By default in python,the program executes from top to bottom by sequentially,sometimes we need to make a decisions like to so the task 5 times repeatedly ,
or one time in a program based on the condition.

This flowcontrol statements help us to achieve this by providing different ways to manage the program execution.

Lets see the real time applications.
Example:In shopping app
1.checks the customer credentials to login ---->Here we use the conditional statements
after login 
2.Browse all the available products  and add them to cart ---->Use Looping statements (To perform same task,multiple times)
3.Skip if you found any out of stock products --->jumping statements


Example 2:In ATM app
for login credentials -->conditional statements
for transactions (Check balance,withdraw,deposit,check balance again)-->looping statements
when the user selects the exit by stoping the transaction loop---jumping statements
